   "text": {
    "L1": "Maheshwar is a heritage town on the Narmada. Let us explore its special places.",
    "L2": "Here, the word bank does not mean a money bank. It means the land beside a river.",
    "L3": "Maheshwar has ghats and a fort. Ghats are wide steps going down into a river.",
    "L4": "Queen Ahilyabai Holkar lived and ruled in Maheshwar more than two hundred years ago.",
    "L5": "Weavers make Maheshwari sarees on looms. A loom is the machine, and a weaver is the person.",
    "L6": "Choose question words carefully. Who asks about a person, and where asks about a place.",
    "L7": "For a past question, use did with the action word. Say, Why did you come to Maheshwar?",
    "L8": "Now tap the question word that asks about a person. The host will check your answer."
   },
